## Summary for User

**Phase 0, 0.9, 1, and 2 (partial) are COMPLETE** with 164 passing tests and 0 technical debt.

The proxy server works for transparent HTTPS tunneling. Service routing logic (registry, domain matching, policy enforcement) is complete and tested, but NOT integrated with the proxy.

**What you can do RIGHT NOW:**
```bash
./chaperone init openai
./chaperone run --config chaperone.toml
# In another terminal:
export HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:4010
curl https://api.openai.com/v1/models
# Request tunnels successfully through proxy (transparent tunnel)
```

**What you CANNOT do yet:**
- Inject API credentials (requires MITM implementation + integration - Phase 2 completion)
- Selective TLS termination (requires CA + certificate generation + integration - Phase 2 completion)
- Retrieve secrets from environment/files/keychain (requires secret providers - Phase 3)
- Enforce policies on proxied requests (policy enforcer exists but not integrated)

**Critical gaps:** 7 (CA generation, certificate generation, TLS handshake, MITM integration, secret providers, auth strategies, policy integration)

**Completion:** 22% (3.9/17 phases, 164/~760 estimated total tests)

**Recommendation:** Continue Phase 2 implementation - CA generation (CHAP-5v5) and certificate generation (CHAP-w9q) next - estimated 3-4 work sessions to complete Phase 2
